22:     - Objects are initially separated from each other.
23: 
24:     Rule:
25:     - Crop each object to its sprite.
26:     - Place every sprite so its gray pixel lands on the same output center.
27:     - Crop the final overlay to the smallest bounding box containing all non-black pixels.
28: 
29:     Key insight:
30:     - Gray is a registration mark, not part of a color rule; aligning all gray anchors reveals the
31:       composite object.
32:     """
